KZ2 patch 6048: a texture level that does not fit in the upload ring submits the list first instead of being skipped.

Root cause of the green sky in Corinth River (public KNOWN_ISSUES "green sky"). create_texture_mipped staged each
level in the per-frame upload ring (UPLOAD_SIZE, 64 MB) and, when the level did not fit in what was left, hit
`break`: the copy was never recorded, the new D3D12 resource kept its initial zeros, the cache entry still pointed at
it and the guest bytes' hash never changed, so the texture was never uploaded again. Killzone 2's first level frame
decodes thousands of textures (the cache goes from 32 to 8192 entries within one 32-frame window) and the sky
panorama (0x092A0000, DXT5 2048x512, 1 MB) came after the ring had filled: it sampled 0 in R, G and A, the sky
shader's YCoCg decode turned that into (0, 3, 0)/255, and post made it green. create_texture_cube and
create_texture_3d had the same check (returning NULL, so the texture bound white for good).

Fix: libs/video/rsx_upload_ring.h (pure, host test tools/runtime/test_upload_ring.sh) decides fit / submit first /
too big; ld_upload_take submits the list (new flush reason LD_FLUSH_UPLOAD_RING, "upring" in [perf-flush]) and
stages at 0, as ld_gv_upload_rows and the retire queue already do. Textures are resolved before the draw sets its
render targets, pipeline and root signature (texture_srv_slot), and a flush invalidates the state memo, so the
draw re-records its state on the new list. One [tex-upload] line per submit (first 32, then every 256th) names the
guest texture; a level larger than the whole ring is still not uploaded but is now reported.
Also an upstream candidate (the check is in ps3recomp's live draw).

